# Keeps local build output, dependencies and tooling state out of the image build context. The
# Dockerfile copies whole directories (repsy-frontend/, libs/, repsy-protocols/, core/), so without
# this a developer's local node_modules or generated client would be copied over the freshly
# installed/generated ones in the image build, and a local build would differ from CI.
#
# This is a deny-list on purpose. Do NOT exclude what the Dockerfile copies: core/ (the git
# submodule), entrypoint.sh, every pom.xml, and
# repsy-backend/src/main/resources/openapi/openapi-spec.yaml.
#
# It applies to the main build context only, not to the `openapi-jar` named context that
# release.yml passes (a directory outside the repository, with no .dockerignore of its own).

# VCS and agent tooling (.claude/worktrees holds whole other checkouts)
.git
.claude

# Maven build output, at any depth (core/, libs/*, repsy-protocols/*, repsy-backend/)
**/target

# Frontend: installed dependencies, build output, caches and the git-ignored generated client. The
# frontend-build stage runs pnpm install and the OpenAPI generator itself.
repsy-frontend/node_modules
repsy-frontend/dist
repsy-frontend/.angular
repsy-frontend/coverage
repsy-frontend/src/generated

# e2e harness: the Dockerfile copies nothing from it (this also covers its node_modules,
# test-results, playwright-report and .env)
e2e

# IDE and OS files
.idea
.vscode
*.iml
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
